Please provide some suggestions for what could be added next to this assembler

● Here are some suggestions, roughly ordered by complexity:

  Low complexity:
  - .ifndef directive - complement to .ifdef, straightforward addition
  - .else for conditionals - more expressive conditional assembly
  - .fill count, value - emit N copies of a byte, useful for padding/alignment
  - .align N - align PC to N-byte boundary (emits padding)

  Medium complexity:
  - More expression operators - *, /, &, |, ^ for bit manipulation
  - .incbin "file" - include raw binary data, useful for embedding graphics/data
  - .repeat N / .endrepeat - unroll loops at assembly time
  - Anonymous labels (+, -, or :) - for short forward/backward branches without naming

  Higher complexity:
  - Expression parentheses - LDA #(foo+bar)*2 with proper precedence
  - Segment support - .code, .data, .bss sections with separate address spaces
  - Listing output - generate human-readable assembly listing with addresses/hex
  - Symbol export - output symbol table for use with debuggers/monitors

  Architectural additions:
  - Warning system - non-fatal diagnostics (e.g., "branch could be optimized")
  - .assert expression, "message" - compile-time assertions for defensive coding
  - Scope blocks - { } or .scope/.endscope for explicit label namespacing

  What interests you? The .else/.ifndef would be natural extensions of existing conditional infrastructure. The .repeat would exercise the macro/memory-source machinery in a new way.

